From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:34:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray 3D: keep the pairing across a stream change

When the demuxer sets the base view's stream up again, on a change of
picture size for one, the pairing of the two views was created anew: the
base pictures waiting in it and the dependent view it had read ahead of
the base view were dropped. The dependent pictures are read from the
extension's file once only, so the base pictures they belonged to were
then dropped too, one by one, until the base view passed the last of
them.

The pairing is now kept, and emptied only if the base view moved to
another stream. Only the stream the pairing was set up for, or the one
on the base view's PID 0x1011, is set up with the second view: a second
H.264 stream, a picture in picture, no longer takes the pairing over.

Shared code, unavoidable: the 3D Blu-ray demuxer exists only in
CoreELEC's Kodi (DVDInputStreamBluray, CDemuxMVC, CDemuxStreamSSIF and
their use in DVDDemuxFFmpeg) and has no AML counterpart.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp    | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
index 58da580..26d8bf5 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -2448,7 +2448,13 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
           {
             int mvcIndex;
             AVStream *mvcStream = nullptr;
-            const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream> pExt = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream>(m_pInput);
+            // the second view goes with the stream it was set up for or the base view's PID,
+            // not with a picture in picture
+            const bool baseView =
+                (m_pSSIF && m_pSSIF->GetH264StreamId() == streamIdx) || pStream->id == 0x1011;
+            const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream> pExt =
+                baseView ? std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream>(m_pInput)
+                         : nullptr;
 
             // the extension is opened for the stream it goes with
             if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && !pExt->GetExtentionDemux())
@@ -2456,8 +2462,11 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
 
             if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && pExt->GetExtentionDemux())
             {
-              delete m_pSSIF;
-              m_pSSIF = new CDemuxStreamSSIF();
+              // a stream change keeps the dependent view already read ahead for the base view
+              if (!m_pSSIF)
+                m_pSSIF = new CDemuxStreamSSIF();
+              else if (m_pSSIF->GetH264StreamId() != streamIdx)
+                m_pSSIF->Flush();
               m_pSSIF->SetH264StreamId(streamIdx);
               m_pSSIF->SetBluRay(pExt);
 
